<div class="landing">
  <.marketing_nav current_user={assigns[:current_user]} active={:pricing} />

  <section class="landing-hero pricing-hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="hero-eyebrow">Pricing</span>
      <h1>Free to publish. Paid when you want a domain of your own.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Every site starts free and stays free — there is no trial and nothing expires.
        A license is per site, so you only pay for the ones that need a custom domain
        or a team behind them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pricing-plans" aria-labelledby="plans-title">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="plans-title">Two plans, per site</h2>

    <div class="pricing-grid">
      <article class="pricing-card">
        <header class="pricing-card-head">
          <h3>Free</h3>
          <p class="pricing-amount">{@free_price}<span>forever</span></p>
          <p class="pricing-sub">Everything you need to write and publish.</p>
        </header>

        <ul class="pricing-list">
          <li>Unlimited posts and pages</li>
          <li>Write in Markdown or HTML</li>
          <li>Themes from the marketplace, or upload your own</li>
          <li>A <code>yoursite.masthead.site</code> address</li>
          <li>Automatic HTTPS</li>
          <li>Image and file uploads</li>
          <li>Tags and drafts</li>
          <li>Import an existing Hugo site</li>
        </ul>

        <.link
          :if={is_nil(assigns[:current_user])}
          navigate={~p"/signup"}
          class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg pricing-action"
        >
          Create your site
        </.link>
        <.link
          :if={assigns[:current_user]}
          navigate={~p"/sites"}
          class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg pricing-action"
        >
          Open dashboard
        </.link>
      </article>

      <article class="pricing-card pricing-card-best">
        <header class="pricing-card-head">
          <h3>
            Paid
            <span :if={@saving} class="pill pill-ok">
              Save {@saving} a year
            </span>
          </h3>
          <p class="pricing-amount">
            {@monthly_price}<span>per month</span>
          </p>
          <p class="pricing-sub">
            or {@yearly_price} billed yearly. Cancel any time.
          </p>
        </header>

        <ul class="pricing-list">
          <li class="pricing-list-head">Everything in Free, plus:</li>
          <li>Your own custom domain — apex or subdomain</li>
          <li>TLS certificates provisioned automatically</li>
          <li>Invite collaborators to the site</li>
        </ul>

        <.link
          :if={is_nil(assigns[:current_user])}
          navigate={~p"/signup"}
          class="btn btn-primary btn-lg pricing-action"
        >
          Start free, upgrade later
        </.link>
        <.link
          :if={assigns[:current_user]}
          navigate={~p"/sites"}
          class="btn btn-primary btn-lg pricing-action"
        >
          Choose a site to upgrade
        </.link>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="pricing-foot">
      Masthead is open source. You can always
      <a href="https://github.com/dijkstrasoftware/masthead" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        run it yourself
      </a>
      instead.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-faq" aria-labelledby="pricing-faq-title">
    <h2 class="section-title" id="pricing-faq-title">Questions about billing</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <h3>Is the free plan really free?</h3>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Yes. A free site has no expiry date and no card on file. It keeps working
          indefinitely on its masthead.site address.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <h3>Do I pay per account or per site?</h3>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Per site. You can run several sites from one account and license only the
          ones that need a custom domain or collaborators.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <h3>What happens if I cancel?</h3>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          The site stays licensed until the period you already paid for runs out, then
          returns to the free plan. Your content is untouched.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <h3>How do I change or cancel my plan?</h3>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          From the site's Settings page, under License. That opens the billing portal
          where you can switch plans, update your card, or cancel.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-cta">
    <div class="cta-card">
      <h2>Start publishing.</h2>
      <p>Create a site for free and upgrade only when you need your own domain.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <.link :if={assigns[:current_user]} navigate={~p"/sites"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          Open dashboard
        </.link>
        <.link
          :if={is_nil(assigns[:current_user])}
          navigate={~p"/signup"}
          class="btn btn-primary btn-lg"
        >
          Create your site
        </.link>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer current_user={assigns[:current_user]} />
</div>
